      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T23:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hardcoding `-ownerin:\"Service Users\"` in client-side default queries introduces a hard failure mode on Gerrit instances where the `Service Users` group does not exist, was renamed, or was deleted. `ChangeQueryBuilder.parseGroup()` throws `QueryParseException: Group Service Users not found`, causing the search endpoint to return HTTP 400 and breaking the default views entirely.\n\nAdditionally, `ownerin:` on internal groups expands into a boolean OR over every account in that group (`NOT (owner:id1 OR owner:id2 ...)`). On instances with dozens or hundreds of service accounts, this generates large Lucene boolean queries on every home page and header link navigation.\n\nShould this instead be backed by a first-class search predicate (e.g. `is:serviceuser` / `is:bot` that evaluates safely) or made configurable server-side via `gerrit.config` rather than hardcoded in the frontend?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b7277d3d1405b09b842fcb1ac42252019c6d577d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ec552f6_8f93928a",
        "filename": "polygerrit-ui/app/elements/core/gr-main-header/gr-main-header.ts",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1030207
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T23:17:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Excluding service users unconditionally from the default \u0027Open\u0027 view hides changes created by automation that explicitly require human review (e.g. dependency bump bots like Renovate/Dependabot, translation syncs, autorollers, toolchain uprevs, and automated cherry-picks). Reviewers relying on the Open changes list to discover and triage incoming work will no longer see these changes without manually overriding the search query.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b7277d3d1405b09b842fcb1ac42252019c6d577d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
